question:
Square $ ABCD $ has side length $10$. Point $E$ is on $\overline{BC}$, and the area of $ \triangle ABE $ is $40$. What is $ BE $? [asy]size(4cm);
pair A,B,C,D,E;
A=(0,0);
B=(0,50);
C=(50,50);
D=(50,0);
E = (30,50);
draw(A--B);
draw(B--E);
draw(E--C);
draw(C--D);
draw(D--A);
draw(A--E);
dot(A);
dot(B);
dot(C);
dot(D);
dot(E);
label("$A$",A,SW);
label("$B$",B,NW);
label("$C$",C,NE);
label("$D$",D,SE);
label("$E$",E,N);
[/asy]

$ABCD$ is a rectangle whose area is 12 square units. How many square units are contained in the area of trapezoid $EFBA$?

[asy]

size(4cm,4cm);

for(int i=0; i < 4; ++i){
for(int k=0; k < 5; ++k){
draw((0,i)--(4,i));
draw((k,0)--(k,3));
} }

draw((0,0)--(1,3));
draw((3,3)--(4,0));

label("$A$",(0,0),SW);
label("$B$",(4,0),SE);
label("$C$",(4,3),NE);
label("$D$",(0,3),NW);
label("$E$",(1,3),N);
label("$F$",(3,3),N);

[/asy]

The fenced area of a yard is a 15-foot by 12-foot rectangular region with a 3-foot by 3-foot square cut out, as shown. What is the area of the region within the fence, in square feet?

[asy]draw((0,0)--(16,0)--(16,12)--(28,12)--(28,0)--(60,0)--(60,48)--(0,48)--cycle);
label("15'",(30,48),N);
label("12'",(60,24),E);
label("3'",(16,6),W);
label("3'",(22,12),N);
[/asy]

Sets $A$ and $B$, shown in the Venn diagram, are such that the total number of elements in set $A$ is twice the total number of elements in set $B$. Altogether, there are 3011 elements in the union of $A$ and $B$, and their intersection has 1000 elements. What is the total number of elements in set $A$?

[asy]
label("$A$", (2,67));
label("$B$", (80,67));
draw(Circle((30,45), 22));
draw(Circle((58, 45), 22));
label("1000", (44, 45));
[/asy]
